<title>TURKEY: Turk Netas H1 net profit up by half.</title>
<headline>Turk Netas H1 net profit up by half.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 2,531.51  vs   1,620.65</p>
<p>    Net profit		  3,157.81  vs   2,021.60</p>
<p>    Net sales		  16,111.47  vs   6,626.94</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  4,346.21  vs   2,055.37</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	1,409.84  vs   1,361.92</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	 572.58  vs     264.86</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 197.83  vs	16.89</p>
<p>    Total debts		11,145.65  vs   4,721.38</p>
<p>    Equity		     12,712.57  vs   6,823.99</p>
<p>    Capital		     1,247.40  vs   1,247.40</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish communications equipment producer Netas Northern Electric Telekomunikasyon AS is owned 53.05 percent byNorthern Telecom Intl Finance BV.</p>
<p>The company recently said it signed a $50 million contract with wireless operator Multi Links Ltd to improve Nigeria's telecommunications system.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
